                                    <h1>EdTech Platform Development: Global Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>EdTech is one of the fastest-consolidating categories globally after the 2021-2022 correction — winners now focus on outcomes, unit economics, and defensible content moats. Here is what a modern EdTech platform looks like across K-12, higher-ed, upskilling, and test-prep verticals.</p>
                                    <h2>Category Sub-Types</h2>
                                    <p><strong>K-12 supplemental:</strong> after-school content, live classes, homework help.<br><strong>Higher-ed:</strong> LMS, MOOC, cohort courses.<br><strong>Test-prep:</strong> JEE / NEET / CAT / GRE / SAT / IELTS / TOEFL.<br><strong>Upskilling / professional:</strong> tech skills, business skills, certifications.<br><strong>Language learning:</strong> Duolingo pattern.<br><strong>Executive education:</strong> higher-touch, cohort-based, higher-priced.</p>
                                    <h2>Common Feature Set</h2>
                                    <ul><li>Course catalog + discovery</li><li>Video streaming + adaptive bitrate</li><li>Live classes (WebRTC or Zoom SDK)</li><li>Interactive exercises + assessments</li><li>AI tutoring / doubt-solving</li><li>Progress tracking + gamification</li><li>Certificates + credentials</li><li>Payment + subscription</li><li>Parent portal (K-12)</li><li>Analytics for learners + institutions</li></ul>
                                    <h2>AI Features That Matter</h2>
                                    <p>Doubt-solving chatbot (2-3x engagement lift on test-prep). Auto-graded practice with feedback. Personalized learning paths. AI-generated practice questions from content. Voice-based conversation practice for language learning.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>MVP (14-22 weeks):</strong> ₹25-60 lakh / $30K-72K.<br><strong>Growth build (22-36 weeks):</strong> ₹80 lakh - 2 Cr / $96K-240K.<br><strong>Enterprise (36-52 weeks):</strong> ₹2-5 Cr / $240K-600K.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Notes</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> Test-prep massive (JEE / NEET / CAT). Byju's collapse created opening for smaller focused players. AOV ₹1,500-50,000.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> K-12 supplemental, IB / IGCSE support, university prep. English + Arabic content.<br><strong>USA:</strong> Test-prep (SAT / MCAT / LSAT), professional (Coursera / edX pattern), K-12 supplemental.<br><strong>UK:</strong> A-level prep, university applications, professional qualifications.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> ATAR prep, professional certification.</p>

